---
scope: "The fingerprint bus contract: the closed-loop semantic template-set push (the service publishes a desired set, the device owns the whole mechanism and answers with one semantic message), the three device-state heartbeats, the two push-time validations, the UUID receipt algorithm, the failure obligations, and the surviving non-push surfaces — device addressing, the retained device announce carrying capabilities(), the commandless match and its three-valued auth_event, the enrollment command and its cancel, the on-the-wire failure taxonomy, and the greppable list of what never crosses. Every off-device operation is a message, never a method call, and the device is the cheapest node that owns its mechanism."
