**Version**: 1.0
**Status**: Draft — the push contract conforms to the corrected device-side shape: one semantic push, the device owns the whole mechanism, no RPC surface. The reconciliation RPC messages of the original (occupancy, roster stamp, template audit, delete-slot, empty, write-template as a wire verb) are deleted; the push owns them inside the device. Slot-allocation corrected: a physical slot index never crosses the bus, the push carries an ORDERED list of logical (person, ordinal) entries plus the small role-to-capability table, the device assigns slots by install order and builds its bridge, and the slot-grant is dissolved. The auth_event is ruled: the device publishes a three-valued outcome (granted, denied, unrecognized) with all three published, on the local bus and uplinked to ComposeBus, retiring the thin user_detected/access_granted pair; the local ring hides denied and unrecognized as one red. No hashing anywhere. Roster-is-push is ruled; capability-binding, enroll-is-device-addressed, the delete-failure class map, and the enroll-readback shape are proposed for the architect.
